{"version":1,"project":{"name":"Lagtrain (WIP)","bpm":147,"key":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"timeSignNom":4,"timeSignDen":4,"phraseLength":4,"patterns":[{"id":0,"name":"Flute call 1","label":"🪈?","color":{"r":205,"g":171,"b":143},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"C","accidental":0},"quality":""},{"root":{"letter":"B","accidental":0},"quality":"m"}],"notes":"This call and response motif is an iconic part of Lagtrain. The song starts and ends with it, and it's used after every instance of the chorus throughout the song.\n\nMelodically, it bounces between the 1st, 5th, and 2nd degrees (E, B, F#), and sometimes jumps to the flat 7th. The lack of 3rds and 6ths give it an airy, neutral, distant and apathetic feel, much like the monochrome video that comes with it.\n\nThere's very little syncopation at first. It hits the all the four beats without accenting offbeats. No syncopated looseness in the flute melody or the chorus. Lagtrain contrasts this rigid, on-beat rhythm with a lot of syncopation in the A and B sections."},{"id":1,"name":"Flute call 2","label":"🪈?","color":{"r":205,"g":171,"b":143},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"quality":"m"},{"root":{"letter":"G","accidental":0},"quality":""}],"notes":""},{"id":2,"name":"Flute response 1","label":"🪈!","color":{"r":205,"g":171,"b":143},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"C","accidental":0},"quality":""},{"root":{"letter":"B","accidental":0},"quality":"m"}],"notes":""},{"id":3,"name":"Flute response 2","label":"🪈!","color":{"r":205,"g":171,"b":143},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"quality":"m"},{"root":{"letter":"G","accidental":0},"quality":""}],"notes":""},{"id":4,"name":"Chorus 1","label":"🚃1","color":{"r":153,"g":193,"b":241},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"C","accidental":0},"quality":""},{"root":{"letter":"B","accidental":0},"quality":"m"}],"notes":"The chorus melody starts by strongly hinting at the 5th, 1st and 2nd degrees, contouring a suspended chord instead of the usual 1-3-5 of the tonic chord. But it does climb to the flat 3rd degree from the 2, then stepping down from the 5 to the 1 on every beat. This creates a temporary Aeolian sound that some may call immaculate.\n\n\"離れ離れの街を繋ぐ列車は\" accents every beat and the &s of 2 and 4, like a rigid march. It's almost surprising to see a modern pop song that starts with so little syncopation in the chorus. Rhythmic contrast falls mostly on the piano chord stab on the & of 3."},{"id":5,"name":"Chorus 4","label":"🚃4","color":{"r":153,"g":193,"b":241},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"quality":"m"},{"root":{"letter":"G","accidental":0},"quality":""}],"notes":"\"行ってしまったね\" and \"\" starts the same rhythm half a beat earlier, as if it the train really did go a bit earlier than anticipated."},{"id":6,"name":"Chorus 2","label":"🚃2","color":{"r":153,"g":193,"b":241},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"quality":"m"},{"root":{"letter":"G","accidental":0},"quality":""}],"notes":""},{"id":7,"name":"Chorus 7","label":"🚃7","color":{"r":153,"g":193,"b":241},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"C","accidental":0},"quality":""},{"root":{"letter":"B","accidental":0},"quality":"m"}],"notes":"ポケットで握りしめて breaks out of the march-like rhythm and divides the rhythm into groups of three eighth notes. Very loose and syncopated\n\n"},{"id":8,"name":"Chorus 8","label":"🚃8","color":{"r":153,"g":193,"b":241},"chords":[{"root":{"letter":"E","accidental":0},"quality":"m9"}],"notes":"This measure doesn't play the G chord. It has a little bit of silence ending the mellower intro chorus. This contrast makes the start of the upcoming *real* chorus much stronger."}],"timeline":[{"type":"pause","duration":3.35},{"type":"section","name":"flute intro"},{"type":"measure","pattern":0},{"type":"measure","pattern":1},{"type":"measure","pattern":2},{"type":"measure","pattern":3},{"type":"section","name":"introサビ"},{"type":"measure","pattern":4},{"type":"measure","pattern":6},{"type":"measure","pattern":4},{"type":"measure","pattern":5}